{"strongs": "H4758", "word": "מַרְאֶה", "translit": "mar.eh", "root": "קשש", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "sight, appearance, vision", "definition": "מַרְאֶה 102 noun masculine Exod 3:3 sight, appearance, vision ; — ׳ מ absolute Gen 12:11 +; construct מַרְאֵה Deut 28:34 +; suffix מַרְאֵהוּ Joel 2:4 +, מַרְאֶהָ Lev 13:4 +; apparently plural construct מַרְאֵי Eccl 11:9 ( Kö ii. 1, 112 ), suffix (probably in fact singular Ges 93 ss ) מַרְאַיִח Song 2:14 (twice in verse), מַרְאֵיהֶן Nah 2:5 +, etc.; — 1. Psalms \\ \\ a. sight, phenomenon, spectacle Exod 3:3 ( J ). \\ \\ b. appearance ׳ נֶחְמָד לְמ Gen 2:9 ( J ) desirable in appearance , ׳ גָּדוֺל לְמ Josh 22:10 appearance of man (or woman), Judg 13:6 (twice in verse) (angel), Isa 52:14 (servant of ׳ י ), Song 5:15 ; Dan 8:15 ; Dan 10:18 = outward person (opposed to inner man) 1Sam 16:7 visible form Song 2:14 (twice in verse); Dan 1:13 (twice in verse); Dan 1:15 ׳ בְּמ Num 12:8 ( E ; so read ⅏ ᵐ5 ᵑ6 ᵑ7 Di , for ᵑ0 מַרְאֶה ), i.e. in personal presence ( < Ew Pat Hpt {abbrev } לֹא בְמ ); כְּמַרְאֵה סוּסִים מַרְאֵהוּ Joel 2:4 of crocodile Job 41:2 ׳ כְּבוֺד י ׳ מ Exod 24:17 ( P ), הַנֶּגַע ׳ מ Lev 13:3 , אֵֿשׁ ׳ מ Num 9:15 ; Num 9:16 , בָּרָק ׳ מ Dan 10:6 +; especially Ezekiel appearance person or of thing (27 t., sometimes redundant), Dan 1:5 ; Dan 1:13 ; Dan 1:26 ; Dan 8:2 ; Dan 10:1 +, מָתְנָיו ׳ מִמּ Dan 1:27 (twice in verse); Dan 8:2 (|| מִמָּתְנָיו ) of beauty וִיפֵה מַרְאֶה fair of appearance Gen 39:6 ( J ; + יְפֵהתֹֿאַר ), compare 1Sam 17:42 (read עֶלֶם [q. v.] for עִם ); feminine ׳ (אִשָּׁה) יְפַתמֿ Gen 12:11 ( J ), Gen 29:17 ( E ; + יְפַת תּאַֹר ), 2Sam 14:27 of kine ׳ יְפוֺת (הַ)מ Gen 41:2 ; Gen 41:4 ( E ), opposed to ׳ רָעוֺת (הַ)מ v Gen 41:3 v Gen 41:4 , מַרְאֵיהֶן רַע v Gen 41:21 (all E ); of women also ׳ טֹבַת מ Gen 24:16 ; Gen 26:7 (both J ), 2Sam 11:2 ; Esth 1:11 ; Esth 2:3 ; Esth 2:7 , ׳ טוֺבוֺת מ Esth 2:2 of boys ׳ טוֺבֵי מ Dan 1:4 , compare ׳ מ alone in וְנֶחְמְדֵהוּ ׳ לֹאמֿ (of suffering servant of ׳ י ) Isa 53:2 ׳ אִישׁ מ 2Sam 23:21 (but read as || 1Chr 11:23 אִישׁ מִדָּה We Dr and others). \\ \\ c. appearance, sight, vision Num 8:4 ( P ). 2. in general what is seen , עֵינָיו ׳ מ Isa 11:3 i.e. what his outward eyes see (compare 1Sam 16:7 1 b), עֵינֶיהָ ׳ לִמ Ezek 23:16 , עְינֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר תִּרְאֶה ׳ מ Deut 28:34 ; Deut 28:67 , ׳ לְכָלמֿ עֵינֵי הַכֹּהֵן Lev 13:12 ( P ). 3. specifically a. (supernatural) vision (in Ezekiel, Daniel; often accusative of congnate meaning with verb with ראה ): Ezek 8:4 ; Ezek 11:24 ; Ezek 43:3 (3 t. in verse), read also מַרְאֵה הָרֶכֶב v Ezek 43:3 (for מַרְאוֺת see I. מַרְאָה above); ׳ בַּמּ Ezek 11:24 ; Dan 8:16 ; Dan 8:27 ; Dan 9:23 ; Dan 10:1 ׳ מ הָעֶרֶב וְהַבֹּקֶר Dan 8:26 . 4. sight, vision = power of seeing (and enjoying), late: עֵינַיִם ׳ מ Eccl 6:9 , הַלֵךְ בְּדַרְּכֵי לִבְּךָ וּבְמַרְאֵי עֵינֶיךָ Eccl 11:9 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7668')\">BDB7668</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H4758')\">H4758</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7667')\">BDB7667</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB7669')\">BDB7669</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>מַרְאֶה</bdbheb><sub>102</sub> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Exod 3:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,3,3)\">Exod 3:3</ref></sup> <highlightword>sight, appearance, vision</highlightword>; — <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>מ</bdbheb> absolute <ref ref=\"Gen 12:11\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(1,12,11)\">Gen 12:11</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>מַרְאֵה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 28:34\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,34)\">Deut 28:34</ref> +; suffix <bdbheb>מַרְאֵהוּ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Joel 2:4\" b=\"29\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(29,2,4)\">Joel 2:4</ref> +, <bdbheb>מַרְאֶהָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Lev 13:4\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"13